{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the high priest</b> who is greater than his brothers in build, in strength, in wealth, in wisdom, and in years." "<b>He pours</b> two instances, and the other is ונהר יוצק יסודם — teaches that the anointing oil that Moses made flowed like a river, and from it they anointed all the kings." "<b>To wear</b> two instances, and the other is ובגד ללבוש (and a garment to wear) — as we expound: let him grow more than his brothers, and this is it: once his hand is filled to wear the garments, then ונתן לי לחם לאכול ובגד ללבוש (and he gave me bread to eat and a garment to wear)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:12.862935566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}